Sylvester Stallone 's classic film &#x201C; Rocky &#x201D; premiered half a century ago.

To mark the occasion, artist John Rivoli has released a new book, &#x201C;The Fine Art Of Rocky: An Artistic Tribute From Screen To Canvas,&#x201D; published by Insight Editions.

The book features rare and never-before-seen original Rocky paintings by Rivoli, an official MGM/Amazon Rocky artist. Related Stories Jeff Goldblum Breaks Into 'Wicked' Song While Reflecting on His 'Unexpectedly Enduring Career' at Marrakech: 'You Just Follow Your Curiosity and Your Heart' How 'Backrooms' Artisans Transformed YouTube Series Into Cinema’s Favorite Liminal Space Using 30,000 Square Feet of Sets and Four Sound Stages

Part art book and part analysis of the six Rocky films, the book invites fans to revisit the iconic franchise through Rivoli&#x2019;s collection of large-scale original paintings and iconic posters, seeing the beloved character in a whole new light. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Rocky takes center stage in this deluxe book, with over 70 of Rivoli's paintings, posters and other unique artworks highlighting unforgettable moments from the films presented in original and unique perspectives as well as art collaborations with Stallone.

Rivoli said, &#x201C;This book represents a lifetime of training &#x2014; for this moment, for this story, for this opportunity to reinterpret Rocky through my own artistic lens.&#x201D;

Speaking with Variety, Rivoli pointed to two pieces featured in the book. The first, &#x201C;Alone in the Ring,&#x201D; is something that holds a special place in his heart. &#x201C;I struggled with how to tell this story visually. I knew that to capture the true significance of the moment, I had to make Rocky small on the canvas. As an artist, that&#x2019;s a difficult decision when you know collectors want a large, commanding image of Rocky hanging on their walls.&#x201D;

Rivoli says the painting wasn&#x2019;t about making Rocky larger than life. &#x201C;It was about showing him surrounded by something much bigger than himself. The ring is enormous, the arena is vast, and the towering image of Apollo Creed dominates the space. Everything around Rocky is larger than he is, emphasizing just how small and alone he feels in that moment.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

It's also a turning point in the film as Rocky's goal shifts from wanting to win the fight to something far more meaningful: going the distance and proving to himself that he&#x2019;s not just another bum from the neighborhood.

&#x201C;That realization is the emotional heart of the story, and it&#x2019;s what I wanted the painting to communicate.&#x201D;

Another meaningful work of art is &#x201C;The Chosen One.&#x201D; Rivoli reveals the original hangs in Stallone's home. He says, &#x201C;It captures the very foundation of the film and the character study that Sylvester Stallone so brilliantly establishes in its opening moments. 'Rocky' begins with an image of Jesus. The camera slowly pans down, revealing the word 'Resurrection,' before ultimately introducing us to Rocky Balboa. In that beautifully constructed sequence, we&#x2019;re being told something profound: we&#x2019;re about to witness the resurrection or redemption of this man.&#x201D; He adds, &#x201C;I find that moment incredibly powerful and I wanted to capture its spiritual and emotional significance on canvas.&#x201D;

&#x201C;My hope is that readers don&#x2019;t just experience the film again, but feel it in a way they never have before &#x2014; as if they&#x2019;re seeing Rocky for the very first time. If it moves them, if it reveals something new, then I&#x2019;ve done what I set out to do.&#x201D;

This richly illustrated volume reimagines Rocky as an immersive artistic celebration, bringing moments from screen to canvas, which invites fans to experience the iconic character in a bold new light across his 50-year legacy.

Guitarist Andy Taylor , whose tenure in England&#x2019;s glammy, pop-savvy rock band Duran Duran coincided with the group&#x2019;s commercial pinnacle of the early &#x2018;80s, died of prostate cancer at his home on Monday while surrounded by family. He was 65.

In a statement shared with Variety , Taylor's wife Tracey said on behalf of their family, "To the world, Andy was a brilliant guitarist, but to us, he was the most wonderful husband, a loving dad and the proudest grandfather. He was the rock of our family. For all the incredible experiences music brought him, family always came first. Nothing made him happier than having us all together, and no matter how far music took him, his heart was always at home." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories David Fincher Explains AI Use in ‘Cliff Booth’ and How AI Can Be Used on Film Sets to Reduce The Amount of Takes but Still Have ‘Real Human Beings’ Vijay Sethupathi's 'Maharaja' Producer Confirms Hollywood Remake Approach as WAVES Film Bazaar Panel Weighs Whether Indian IP Can Travel

Duran Duran added, "Andy was there at the very beginning of our story. From the moment he arrived in Birmingham from the North East with a guitar and an unshakeable belief in what we could become, he brought an indelible fire and swagger to our music. His playing drove the songs that took us around the world, and with a dry wit that was matched only by his wonderfully unsentimental, no-nonsense outlook on life he kept us grounded and gave the band its edge through the extraordinary years that followed."

Taylor, who was diagnosed with stage 4 metastatic prostate cancer in 2018, had opted out on appearing at the group&#x2019;s November 2022 induction into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame, citing a decline in his health in a statement.

He said, &#x201C;Although my current condition is not immediately life-threatening there is no cure&#x2026;. Recently I was doing OK after some very sophisticated life-extending treatment, that was until a week or so ago when I suffered a setback, and despite the exceptional efforts of my team, I had to be honest in that both physically and mentally, I would be pushing my boundaries.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Duran Duran had been in existence for two years in the Midlands city of Birmingham when Taylor &#x2014; then a 19-year-old veteran seeking new opportunities after successfully touring British army bases in Europe with a cover band &#x2014; spotted a April 1980 Melody Maker classified ad seeking a &#x201C;Live Wire Guitarist.&#x201D;

He wrote in &#x201C;Wild Boy,&#x201D; his candid and frequently sensational 2008 autobiography, &#x201C;[The ad] cited Mick Ronson of the Spiders From Mars and Steve Jones of the Sex Pistols as musical influences so I thought it looked worth a call.&#x201D;

After a successful audition, Taylor became a member of the quintet, which became a popular fixture at the Birmingham club the Rum Runner. Sporting extravagant coiffs and makeup &#x2014; &#x201C;We&#x2019;d end up discussing cosmetics with the girls,&#x201D; Taylor later wrote &#x2014; the band was lumped in with Britain&#x2019;s New Romantic movement of the early &#x2018;80s. After only eight months with Taylor in the lineup, the act was signed by EMI.

Duran Duran &#x2014; whose early compositions were credited to all five group members &#x2014; became a nearly instant success in the U.K. Its third single &#x201C;Girls on Film&#x201D; (No. 5) helped push its self-titled debut album to No. 3. The 1982 followup album &#x201C;Riot&#x201D; spawned the hits &#x201C;Hungry Like the Wolf&#x201D; (No. 5) and the eponymous single (No. 9). Its first No. 1 single &#x201C;Is There Something I Should Know&#x201D; was issued in 1983.

The band was among the first beneficiaries of Stateside exposure on MTV, the then-new cable network that broke through with wall-to-wall airing of videos; their lavish clips, handsomely directly by former 10cc members Kevin Godley and Lol Creme and the prolific Russell Mulcahy, captured eyes with their lush cinematography, scantily clad models and expensive location shoots in exotic locales like Sri Lanka and Antigua. Three Duran Duran singles reached the U.S. top five in 1982-83.

Taylor noted in his memoir that those videos often found the band members risking life and limb: &#x201C;They were enormous fun to make &#x2014; even if it nearly killed us at times. I&#x2019;m not joking! Several of us risked being drowned, we narrowly escaped being trampled by a crazed elephant, and we were forced to flee one shoot after being threatened by four thousand angry monks.&#x201D; Unsurprisingly, Duran Duran&#x2019;s only Grammy Awards, both presented in 1986, were for best short form music video and (for &#x201C;Duran Duran,&#x201D; a compilation of their first 12 clips) best long form music video. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

By 1983, the act was big enough in England to headline a London charity benefit attended by Prince Charles and Princess Diana, who told its members, &#x201C;I don&#x2019;t need any introductions to these boys. I know exactly who they are.&#x201D; Their album of that year, Seven and the Ragged Tiger,&#x201D; shot to No. 1 in the U.K. and No. 8 in the U.S.

However, by 1984, when the singles &#x201C;The Reflex&#x201D; and &#x201C;The Wild Boys&#x201D; reached No. 1 and No. 2 respectively in both the U.K. and the U.S., the band&#x2019;s hard-partying, notoriously debauched lifestyle was beginning to shred their reputation; a story in the Fleet Street tabloid the Sun detailed stories of extreme cocaine abuse &#x2014; later verified by Taylor, who, with bassist John Taylor (no relation), was the drug&#x2019;s most enthusiastic user. Additional turmoil came into the guitarist&#x2019;s life that year after his wife Tracey suffered a postpartum psychotic episode following the birth of their son Andrew.

Wrung out from a grueling recording and touring schedule and increasingly debilitated by their drug habits, Andy and John Taylor made a lateral move into a new quartet, the Power Station, which also featured white-soul vocalist Robert Palmer and Chic&#x2019;s drummer Tony Thompson. Produced by Thompson&#x2019;s band mate Bernard Edwards, its self-titled 1985 debut reached No. 6 in the U.S. and No. 12 in the U.K. (A long-delayed 1996 sequel, with Edwards standing in on bass for John Taylor, then in rehab, failed to chart.)

By the time Duran Duran appeared at the U.S. incarnation of the transatlantic, internationally televised benefit concert Live Aid in July 1985, the original lineup of the group was reaching the end of its tether. Taylor wrote in his memoir, &#x201C;John and I were in a dark place&#x2026;.[W]e were dying inside. We were tired of twenty-four-hour attention, tired of drinking and taking drugs, haggard from the lifestyle we had once aspired to.&#x201D;

Exiting the band in 1986, Taylor attempted to clean up his life in Los Angeles and began working with Steve Jones, the former guitarist for the Sex Pistols and himself then newly in recovery. The fruits of their collaboration included &#x201C;Take It Easy,&#x201D; a No. 24 pop hit heard on the soundtrack for the film &#x201C;American Anthem,&#x201D; and the tough &#x201C;I Might Lie,&#x201D; which rose to No. 17 on Billboard&#x2019;s mainstream rock chart. His 1987 solo set &#x201C;Thunder&#x201D; reached No. 46 domestically. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Following occasional work behind Rod Stewart, Taylor rejoined Duran Duran, after an absence of 14 years, for a full reunion of the original band. A successful world tour and a new album, 2004&#x2019;s &#x201C;Astronaut&#x201D; (No. 3 in the U.K., No. 17 in the U.S.), followed. But the guitarist soon became discontent again, and exited a second time in 2006; material he had worked on for a new album was shelved.

&#x201C;I was tired of going over and over the same old creative difficulties and financial tensions,&#x201D; he later wrote, &#x201C;and I was fed up with having blazing rows with our management over what I perceived to be our lack of clear direction&#x2026;.We&#x2019;d ceased to function as a band; it was seriously dysfunctional. We&#x2019;d returned to being five individuals pulling in different directions, just as we&#x2019;d become in the eighties. When it came to sorting out our problems, just like before, we failed to connect.&#x201D;

In 2007-08, Taylor was briefly partnered in RockAffairs.com, a site devoted to the sale and promotion of music by unsigned independent artists.

He was born Feb. 16, 1961, in Tynemouth, Northumberland, and raised nearby Cullercoats.. At 11, he received his first guitar as a Christmas present, and in his teens played with local acts like the Gigolos before touring Europe.

He is survived by wife Tracey and his children Andrew, Isabelle, Bethany and Georgina.

EXCLUSIVE : The Hawk did not make the cut for a second season. Netflix has opted not to renew the freshman golf comedy, co-created, executive produced and headlined by Will Ferrell . The news comes more than four months after The Hawk, SNL alum Ferrell's first TV starring vehicle, premiered on July 16.

The decision fits Netflix's performance vs. cost renewal criteria. The Hawk was believed to be among the most expensive comedy series on Netflix, with its star Ferrell commanding a seven-figure episodic salary. It spent three weeks in Netflix's Global Top 10 for English series, peaking at No.2 with 6.2M views for its first full week, a respectable but not outsized delivery. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The show did not score well with critics, averaging 33% in reviews on Rotten Tomatoes but did better with core Will Ferrell fans for a 65% audience score. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

The Hawk 's fate was telegraphed by co-creator/executive producer Harper Steele during an interview on Late Night with Seth Meyers two weeks ago in which she said, in passing, &#x201C;I was working on a short-lived but probably the best show ever, The Hawk. &#x201D;

Ferrell remains in business with Netflix. Via Gloria Sanchez Productions, he executive produces the streamer's upcoming series All the Rage, Prep as well as Nikki Glaser&#x2019;s first scripted show, developed through Netflix Is a Joke Studios .

Of the comedy series that have released new seasons after The Hawk 's debut, Netflix has renewed Nobody Wants This , whose third season delivered the biggest 2026 opening week for a returning scripted comedy, Tires and freshman A Different World. Leanne is awaiting word on a Season 3 pickup; it's too early for Minimum Wage .

Upcoming Netflix comedy series also include Uncorked, A Hundred Percent and I Suck at Girls.

In The Hawk , Lonnie Hawkins (Ferrell), 2004&#x2019;s number one golfer, struggles on the back nine of his career to recapture his magic. His body says retire, but his heart says he&#x2019;s not done yet. His ex-wife and his son Lance, golf&#x2019;s new golden boy, know he&#x2019;s through. But with one more major to win to complete golf&#x2019;s Grand Slam, Lonnie refuses to believe he&#x2019;s anything other than one stroke away from the greatest comeback in golf history. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In the series, Ferrell reunited with former SNL co-star Molly Shannon who played his foul-mouthed ex-wife. Jimmy Tatro, Fortune Feimster, Luke Wilson, Chris Parnell, Katelyn Tarver and David Hornsby also starred in The Hawk , which was co-created by Ferrell, Steele and Chris Henchy.

Ferrell, Jessica Elbaum and Alix Taylor executive produced for Gloria Sanchez Productions. Rian Johnson, Ram Bergman and Nena Rodrigue were executive producers for T-Street. Henchy, Steele, David Gordon Green and Andrew Guest also executive produced.

Brad Pitt and Angelina Jolie have settled a long-running dispute over the sale of their French winery, a lawsuit that opened the door for the actress to accuse her ex-husband of abusing her and their children.

Both sides on Wednesday moved to dismiss claims against each other. Terms of the settlement weren't disclosed.

&#x201C;We have settled out of court in the best interests of our family and will not be commenting further," said representatives for Jolie and Pitt in a statement. "Any comments in media stories attributed to 'sources' are in fact not coming from either of us, or anyone close to us.&#x201D;

The couple purchased the 1,200-acre winery in the South of France where they married, Ch&#xE2;teau Miraval, in 2008. Jolie planned to sell her half to Pitt in the wake of their divorce, court filings alleged, until negotiations broke down over his insistence that she sign a nondisclosure agreement barring her from publicizing allegations of abuse leading up to their split.

Jolie balked at the ask and instead struck a $64 million deal with billionaire alcohol magnate Yuri Shefler for her half of the winery. Pitt in 2022 filed a lawsuit, claiming that the actress reneged on an unwritten agreement that they wouldn&#x2019;t sell their stakes in the business without the other&#x2019;s consent. That led to a countersuit from Jolie publicizing for the first time abuse allegations against Pitt in a 2016 altercation on a private plane in which she claimed that the actor &#x201C;grabbed her by the head and shook her,&#x201D; &#x201C;choked one of the children&#x201D; and &#x201C;struck another in the face.&#x201D;

At the time, a representative for Pitt denied the allegations. Jolie &#x201C;continues to rehash, revise and reimagine her description of an event that happened 6 years ago by adding completely untrue information each time she fails to get what she wants," the spokesperson said. "Her story is constantly evolving.&#x201D;

Wednesday's settlement ends a contentious case that peeled back the origins of Pitt and Jolie's divorce and hostility between the former couple. Pitt continues to pursue claims against Shefler, who allegedly orchestrated the acquisition in secret alongside Jolie, and Shefler's company Tenute del Mondo, the wine arm of the Stoli Group. The actor seeks a court order allowing him to purchase Jolie's shares in Miraval at the same valuation Shefler acquired them, plus unspecified damages.

A state appeals court earlier this year found that Shefler played a vital role in structuring and finalizing the deal to purchase Miraval. It pointed to him guaranteeing $39 million of the purchase using his own funds, a provision he wouldn&#x2019;t agree to if he wasn&#x2019;t involved in the agreement. Shefler sent three letters to Jolie over the course of the transaction, according to court filings. One thanked her for accepting his offer and assured her that a deal would be made &#x201C;despite personal complications.&#x201D; Another asked Jolie to postpone paying an installment on the purchase due to complications with Pitt.

Since the allegations became public in 2022, Pitt has continued starring in major studio productions, like F1 and Heart of the Beast , maintaining his dual-standing as one of Hollywood's most bankable leading men and a prolific producer of prestige film through Plan B Entertainment. Jolie, meanwhile, momentarily took a step back from acting before earning critical acclaim for her portrayal as Maria Callas in Maria .

In her cross complaint, Jolie detailed a physical altercation with Pitt, with him on one side and her and their children on the other.

&#x201C;Pitt lunged at his own child and Jolie grabbed him from behind to stop him,&#x201D; the complaint stated. &#x201C;To get Jolie off his back, Pitt threw himself backwards into the airplane&#x2019;s seats injuring Jolie&#x2019;s back and elbow. The children rushed in and all bravely tried to protect each other.&#x201D;

At one point, Pitt poured beer on Jolie; at another, he poured beer and wine on the children, the lawsuit alleged. Once the flight landed, Jolie claimed Pitt pushed her when she told him that she and the children were going to a hotel. &#x201C;He also grabbed and shook Jolie by the head and shoulders, causing one of the children to beg, &#x2018;Don&#x2019;t hurt her,'&#x201D; the complaint stated. &#x201C;He let Jolie go, but then called her a &#x2018;bitch,&#x2019; before adding, &#x2018;Fuck you, fuck you all.'&#x201D; Jolie filed for divorce five days later.

The FBI investigated the 2016 altercation but declined to press charges. A redacted report on the case stated that the investigating agent found there was probable cause to pursue a criminal case but that charges would not be filed due to &#x201C; several factors ,&#x201D; according to The New York Times . It described Jolie as being &#x201C;conflicted on whether or not to be supportive of charges.&#x201D;

Pitt was represented by John Berlinksi and Julia Cherlow, partners at Bird Marella, while Jolie was represented by Paul Murphy and Daniel Csillag. Alejandro Brito, who handles media lawsuit for President Trump, represents Shefler.

In the nine months since &#x201C;Gugu&#x2019;s World&#x201D; premiered in Berlin, director Allan Deberton has had only the most &#x201C;joyful experiences.&#x201D; By the time the filmmaker sits down with Variety to discuss the whirlwind, the film has just opened in its home country of Brazil, turning its young star into a phenomenon.

That star is Yuri Gomes, who plays the titular Gugu. The boy is the epitome of freedom, zigzagging across a dirt field with a football, then breaking into a dance sequence the moment he hears the throbbing beats of Brazilian brega music. Yes, those around him judge him, including stern dad Batista (L&#xE1;zaro Ramos), but Gugu is sheltered by the love of grandmother Dilma (Teca Pereira). The two live together in a small town in Cear&#xE1;, their loving home and safe cocoon until the day Dilma&#x2019;s health deteriorates due to a rapidly developing case of Alzheimer&#x2019;s. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories ‘Hold Onto Me’: Myrsini Aristidou’s Debut Feature Proves Power of Reconnection Through Complex, Powerful Father-Daughter Bond Miley Cyrus to Accept CNN Heroes Legacy Award to Dolly Parton

&#x201C;Gugu&#x2019;s World&#x201D; follows Deberton&#x2019;s &#x201C;Pacarrete&#x201D; and reunites the director with screenwriter Andr&#xE9; Ara&#xFA;jo, who originated the story. The tale of this energetic boy resonated deeply with the filmmaker, who knew he needed a &#x201C;great cast&#x201D; to do justice to the &#x201C;responsibility&#x201D; of tackling the issues in the script, from talking about young queerness to dealing with caring responsibilities and progressive disorders. Deberton landed two of Brazil&#x2019;s great screen stars in Ramos and Pereira, but the process of finding Gugu was a much more complex, lengthy operation. The film team saw over 700 kids and eventually found Gomes, a star-in-the-making. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;We needed an actor who had the spirit of Gugu,&#x201D; says producer Karen Castanho of Bi&#xF4;nica Filmes. &#x201C;But today, the great challenge of filming kids is that, because of social media, kids are not very spontaneous. Yuri is the opposite of that.&#x201D;

Deberton worked closely with casting director and AD Luciana Vieira to ensure that not only Gomes but the wider cast of children were &#x201C;very natural.&#x201D; &#x201C;We simply see children being children. We don&#x2019;t see kids acting. I think that&#x2019;s very strong in the film.&#x201D;

The director said it is &#x201C;transformative&#x201D; to work with children. He enjoyed the experience so much that he decided to replicate it for his next project, &#x201C;Adoption,&#x201D; dealing with his personal experience adopting his son. &#x201C;What they put on the screen is very truthful. We need to be open to that gaze, which is pure, intimate, truthful and that makes us feel alive.&#x201D;

The film presented a great challenge to Ramos, an actor-director with decades of experience and one of the most recognizable names in Brazil thanks to his work on telenovelas and films such as &#x201C;Madame Sat&#xE3;&#x201D; and &#x201C;Carandiru.&#x201D; Ramos is more widely known for his loving, well-humored roles, so playing a stern father dealing with internalized homophobia and unable to accept his son was difficult.

&#x201C;My first read of [Batista] was one that is very distant from the dad I aim to be,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;I was looking to villainize that figure, to signal his flaws, like an alert call. But when we started rehearsing, he gained richness and a much more interesting personality, which is this man who does care about his child, who seeks to be closer to his child, but he doesn&#x2019;t have the resources.&#x201D;

Asked about the physicality of his character, who is often contained in contrast to Gugu&#x2019;s penchant for movement, Ramos shared the complex process. During rehearsals, it felt &#x201C;curious&#x201D; to Ramos how he couldn&#x2019;t mimic Gomes&#x2019; movements. The two often danced together or moved together between takes, but Ramos returned to introspection when cameras rolled. &#x201C;It was good to encounter that vitality of his to understand the opposition we&#x2019;d aim for in each scene,&#x201D; he said.

Pereira, on the other hand, was able to imbue Dilma with a lot of herself, such as &#x201C;her joy for life, that animated way of living and the way she cares for her grandson,&#x201D; she noted. The role was still quite different from everything she had done previously, with the experience made even more special thanks to the relationship she developed with Gomes. &#x201C;Luciana Vieira gave us exercises for us to develop that care, to develop a bond,&#x201D; she recalled. &#x201C;It was great. Yuri is an intelligent, clever child, as well as talented.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Working on an indie project always brings a set of challenges, but shooting with a large ensemble cast mostly of children and setting the production in Quixad&#xE1;, a small city in the inland of Cear&#xE1;, added massively to Castanho&#x2019;s plate.

